Operating and Marketing Airline Details

The following fields will be displayed in the check-in email only when the Operating Airline Code and Marketing Airline Code are different in the TripSearch API response:

Operating Airline
Operating Airline Flight Number
Marketing Airline
Marketing Airline Flight Number

These fields will not be displayed in the check-in email when the Operating Airline Code and Marketing Airline Code are the same, as shown in the example below:

Operating Airline Code: WY
Operating Flight Number: 0101
Marketing Airline Code: WY
Marketing Flight Number: 0101
2. Record Locator for Operating Airline

The Record Locator for the Operating Airline will be the PNR that is currently displayed as the Booking Reference in the check-in email.

3. Baggage Allowance

The customer's baggage allowance will be obtained from the GetPassengerData API response using the BagAllowance field. For example:

Bag Allowance: 30 KG
4. Seat Information

Seat information will be displayed alongside the passenger's name only when seat details are available in the TripSearch API response.

If seat information is not available, it will not be displayed in the check-in email.

5. Check-in Details
Check-in Terminal

The check-in terminal will be displayed based on the Terminal information received from the FlightInfo API response.

Example:

Departure Airport: LHR
Terminal: TERMINAL 4
Check-in Airline

The check-in airline will be displayed as "WY" for all passengers.

Check-in Channel

Please confirm what should be displayed for the Check-in Channel field in the check-in email.

